ext-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"African Safari Animal Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[2,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#asian\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Asian Wildlife Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[3,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#rainforest\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Rainforest Animal Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[4,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#savanna\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Savanna & Grassland Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"There is something undeniably majestic about zoo and safari animals. From the thundering hooves of wildebeest across the Serengeti to the silent stalk of a \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"156\",{\"href\":\"/animal/tiger/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Tiger\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" through Asian jungles, these magnificent creatures inspire some of the most powerful and evocative pet names imaginable.\"]}],\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\"]}],\"$L2f\",\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"African Safari Animal Names 🦁\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Africa's wildlife is the stuff of legend. Direct animal names like <strong>Simba</strong> (lion in Swahili), <strong>Duma</strong> (cheetah), <strong>Tembo</strong> (elephant), <strong>Kiboko</strong> (hippopotamus), <strong>Chui</strong> (leopard), <strong>Faru</strong> (rhinoceros) bring authentic African meaning. Swahili nature words: <strong>Mwezi</strong> (moon), <strong>Jua</strong> (sun), <strong>Nyota</strong> (star), <strong>Pori</strong> (wilderness).\"}}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"African place names evoke vast landscapes: <strong>Serengeti</strong>, <strong>Kilimanjaro</strong>, <strong>Sahara</strong>, <strong>Kalahari</strong>, <strong>Zambezi</strong>, <strong>Okavango</strong>, <strong>Ngorongoro</strong>. Safari itself makes a wonderful name: <strong>Safari</strong> — it means 'journey' in Swahili and immediately conjures images of wild adventure.\"}}]\n26:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Asian Wildlife Names 🐅\"]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Asia's diverse wildlife spans from Siberian {tiger}s to Indian {elephant}s to Indonesian {komodo-dragon}s. Indian names: <strong>Sher</strong> (tiger), <strong>Bagheera</strong> (black panther), <strong>Hathi</strong> (elephant), <strong>Mowgli</strong>, <strong>Baloo</strong>, <strong>Akela</strong>, <strong>Raksha</strong>. These Jungle Book names double as literary and wildlife references.\"}}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Southeast Asian wildlife names: <strong>Harimau</strong> (tiger in Malay), <strong>Badak</strong> (rhino), <strong>Gajah</strong> (elephant). Chinese wildlife words: <strong>Long</strong> (dragon), <strong>Hu</strong> (tiger). Japanese: <strong>Tora</strong> (tiger), <strong>Kuma</strong> (bear), <strong>Ryu</strong> (dragon). The names of real Asian animals like <strong>Orangutan</strong> and <strong>Komodo</strong> are powerful names in their own right.\"}}]\n29:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Rainforest Animal Names 🌴\"]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Rainforests pulse with life and color. Amazon-inspired: <strong>Amazon</strong>, <strong>Rio</strong>, <strong>Iguazu</strong>, <strong>Tropic</strong>. Rainforest animal names: <strong>Toucan</strong>, <strong>Macaw</strong>, <strong>Jaguar</strong>, <strong>Anaconda</strong>, <strong>Capybara</strong>, <strong>Tapir</strong>, <strong>Kinkajou</strong>, <strong>Tamarin</strong>, <strong>Marmoset</strong>.\"}}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Portuguese and Spanish wildlife words (Amazon languages): <strong>Onça</strong> (jaguar), <strong>Arara</strong> (macaw), <strong>Boto</strong> (pink river dolphin), <strong>Piranha</strong>, <strong>Sucuri</strong> (anaconda). Exotic plant names: <strong>Bromeliad</strong>, <strong>Orchid</strong>, <strong>Heliconia</strong>, <strong>Passion</strong> (flower).\"}}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Savanna & Grassland Names 🌾\"]}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The world's grasslands stretch across continents. These names evoke wide-open spaces and endless skies. American prairie: <strong>Dakota</strong>, <strong>Cheyenne</strong>, <strong>Prairie</strong>, <strong>Bison</strong>, <strong>Meadow</strong>. South American pampas: <strong>Pampas</strong>, <strong>Gaucho</strong>, <strong>Puma</strong>, <strong>Rhea</strong>. Australian outback: <strong>Outback</strong>, <strong>Kangaroo</strong>, <strong>Dingo</strong>, <strong>Billabong</strong>, <strong>Uluru</strong>.\"}}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Mongolian steppe: <strong>Steppe</strong>, <strong>Gobi</strong>, <strong>Khan</strong>, <strong>Temujin</strong> (Genghis Khan's birth name). These expansive landscape names carry the spirit of freedom, migration, and wild horizons — perfect for pets with adventurous spirits or those who love the outdoors.\"}}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I name a small pet after a large safari animal?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The irony of a tiny hamster named Elephant or a gerbil named Giraffe is genuinely delightful. Contrast between name and pet creates charm and memorable conversation.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are there any cultural considerations when using African names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Using Swahili or other African language names with respect and appreciation is beautiful. Learn the meaning and pronunciation — it shows genuine cultural appreciation and makes the name richer.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What's the most popular safari-inspired pet name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Simba has been one of the most popular pet names globally since The Lion King, closely followed by Nala. Safari and Serengeti are also surprisingly common and well-loved.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should the name match my pet's species?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A lion-inspired name for a cat feels natural, but cross-species naming creates wonderful surprise. A guinea pig named Jaguar or a rabbit named Bison is unexpected and delightful.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"lion\",{\"href\":\"/animal/lion/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm 